# BMW 3 Series E90 four-door saloon, 2005-2012.
#
# The fifth 3-series, the first with the flame-surfaced body and the "Bangle"
# boot lid. The saloon is modelled; the E91 estate, E92 coupe and E93
# convertible are different bodies.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_3_Series_(E90)
#
# Dimensions 4.520 x 1.817 x 1.421 m, wheelbase 2.760 m, for the saloon, from
# the English Wikipedia dimension box, which gives ranges across the four body
# styles and puts the saloon at the lower end of each. Mirrors take the modelled
# width to 2.025 m.
#
# Colours: from the BMW UK 3 Series Saloon price list, March 2009, printed
# page 11, which is a primary UK source:
#   Alpine White            300
#   Jet Black               668
#   Titansilber metallic    354
#   Monacoblau metallic     A35
# The price list establishes UK offering in March 2009, not the full
# production-year range; introduction and withdrawal years for each colour are
# not established. Melbourne Red and Estoril Blue were not confirmed as
# ordinary UK saloon choices and are left out.
# Weights silver 3, black 3, white 2, blue 2, total 10, provisional pending the
# central rebase.
#
# Speed 225 km/h, around the 325i's 240 km/h and the 320i's 220 km/h; the 335i
# and the M3 are not modelled. Comfort 125/518, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 125,
# the same as the E39. Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence, not production: March 2005 intro, retires staggered
# 2020-2023 on a fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-e90.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-e90.dae (63 objects). References:
# citycars/references/bmw-e90/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted low-poly deviations, recorded rather than corrected: the glasshouse
# is more angular than the photographs and the boot and bumper surfaces are
# flatter. The builder flagged these and did not certify Gate B. At 128 px the
# car reads as an E90-shape saloon and the wheel arches sit tight to the tyres,
# so no correction round was spent.

obj=citycar
name=BMW3E90(Titansilber)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=2005
intro_month=3
retire_year=2023
retire_month=6
speed=225
length=3
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=125
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=518

